# The seal is a SHA-256 over bytes, so line endings are part of the contract.
#
# Without this file, a clone on a machine with Git's Windows default
# (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites every .md to CRLF, and the first thing this
# protocol asks a new reader to do — verify the seal on the shipped example —
# fails with a mismatch whose stated remedy is "stop". That is a false positive
# on the flagship guard, on day one, which is how guards get switched off.
#
# This must ship in the initial release. Adding it after adopters have cloned
# re-creates the same mismatch in the other direction.

* text=auto

*.md    text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
LICENSE text eol=lf
